  "notes": [
    "Quiet startup comparison: three EN resets per firmware, echo probes every 500 ms. Host readiness includes serial delivery and probe-interval quantization; BOOT and dictionary I/O times are device measurements.",
    "Dictionary ready host median improved from 19261.2 to 13275.4 ms (31.08%). The shell was already usable earlier; its startup did not improve.",
    "The initial and reopened-serial coexistence attempts each reset the device. Their memory samples spanned Tailscale startup: free PSRAM increased 501 and 499 KiB. Source inspection shows temporary control-connection and 512 KiB response allocations; no per-allocation hardware trace was captured.",
    "Holding serial open during a 60-second settle brought trimmed memory samples within 16 KiB (23135 to 23119 KiB free), passing the unchanged 32 KiB tolerance. That run still failed the unchanged 5% loss limit because the 25 pps font phase lost 10 of 75 echoes. Its 100 pps idle/PAK/font phases had zero loss and Write lost 5 of 180.",
    "All seven postboot 18689235-byte PAK CRC reads matched 74e3b084. No invalid echo payload/checksum was observed. Failed runs are retained and are not claimed as qualification passes.",
    "The SD loader had exited before the postboot coexistence workloads. The source of network loss variability remains unassigned; no regression attribution to the IME change has been established.",
    "The boot overlap attempt finished loading the dictionary before connected IPv4 was reported, so it did not establish dictionary/Wi-Fi overlap.",
    "The tools issue no media-mutation command, but normal background services may persist their own state. No backup was taken this turn as authorized. Only the selected app slot was flashed.",
    "Power loss, hot removal, controlled simultaneous writes and maximum network throughput remain unqualified. Raw serial transcripts are private; reports contain their SHA-256 digests."
  ]
